### Status of two-factor authentication for the logged-in user: methods, whether the organisation requires it, whether e-mail is available
GET {{baseApiPath}}/mfa

### Start the setup - answers a new secret and the otpauth:// address for the QR code
POST {{baseApiPath}}/mfa/setup

### Switch it on with the first code from the authenticator app
# A user who already has a method also gives a code of it as currentCode - a second factor is only added by
# someone who holds the first.
POST {{baseApiPath}}/mfa/enable
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "123456",
  "currentCode": "654321"
}

### Start the e-mail method - sends a code to the address on the account
POST {{baseApiPath}}/mfa/email/setup

### Switch the e-mail method on with the code from the mail (currentCode as for the app, when a method is on already)
POST {{baseApiPath}}/mfa/email/enable
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "123456",
  "currentCode": "654321"
}

### Send a code by e-mail (to set up, to log in with the e-mail method, or to switch a method off)
POST {{baseApiPath}}/mfa/email/send

### Switch a method off (needs a current code of either method) - method is TOTP or EMAIL
POST {{baseApiPath}}/mfa/disable
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "method": "TOTP",
  "code": "123456"
}

### Finish a login that still owes its code (with /mfa/email/send, /users/info and /users/logout the only calls such a session may make)
POST {{baseApiPath}}/mfa/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "123456"
}

### Passkeys: options for creating one (needs a code method to be on) - answer goes to navigator.credentials.create()
POST {{baseApiPath}}/mfa/passkey/setup

### Passkeys: add the one the browser created - credential is PublicKeyCredential.toJSON(), currentCode a code of a method the user has
POST {{baseApiPath}}/mfa/passkey/enable
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "credential": {
    "id": "...",
    "rawId": "...",
    "type": "public-key",
    "response": {
      "clientDataJSON": "...",
      "attestationObject": "..."
    },
    "clientExtensionResults": {}
  },
  "name": "Laptop",
  "currentCode": "123456"
}

### Passkeys: remove one (needs a current code)
POST {{baseApiPath}}/mfa/passkey/7/disable
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "123456"
}

### Passkeys: options for a login that still owes its second step - answer goes to navigator.credentials.get()
POST {{baseApiPath}}/mfa/passkey/login-options

### Passkeys: finish that login with the assertion instead of a code
POST {{baseApiPath}}/mfa/passkey/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "credential": {
    "id": "...",
    "rawId": "...",
    "type": "public-key",
    "response": {
      "clientDataJSON": "...",
      "authenticatorData": "...",
      "signature": "..."
    },
    "clientExtensionResults": {}
  }
}

### Administrator: switch it off for a user who lost the phone (removes the passkeys too)
DELETE {{baseApiPath}}/users/300/mfa
